### What a correct structure looks like (for reference)
The candidate match must persist across iterations, a full match must increment `count` by 1 and *exclude* those characters from the leftover, a mismatch must flush the partial to the leftover and re‑check the current character, and the recursion should run on the leftover only when a match was found:

```java
public int numNestedOccurrences(String string, String word) {
    int count = 0;
    StringBuilder leftover = new StringBuilder();
    StringBuilder building = new StringBuilder();

    for (int i = 0; i < string.length(); i++) {
        char c = string.charAt(i);
        if (building.length() < word.length() && c == word.charAt(building.length())) {
            building.append(c);                 // extend the candidate
            if (building.equals(word)) {        // full match: count it, drop it
                count++;
                building.setLength(0);
            }
        } else {                                 // mismatch: flush partial to leftover,
            leftover.append(building);          // then re-examine this same char
            building.setLength(0);
            i--;
        }
    }
    leftover.append(building);                   // don't lose a trailing partial

    if (count == 0) return 0;                    // base case: nothing more nested
    return count + numNestedOccurrences(leftover.toString(), word);
}
```
